          "valid_to_calendar": "gregorian",
          "confidence": "reviewed",
          "notes": "GPRF government phase on the higher-order French Republic polity begins when CFLN adopted its name on 3 June 1944. Provisional authorities continued through the constitutional transition on 24 December 1946, when the Fourth Constitution entered into force. This date is the common institutional transition boundary; daily granularity does not mean the two governments operated throughout all hours of 24 December. De Gaulle's personal term (9 Sep 1944–20 Jan 1946) is only a subset and remains unchanged. The regime is not retrospectively conflated with Vichy de facto power or treated as a separate sovereign Polity."
