          "notes": "French Fourth Republic constitutional-regime period begins 24 December 1946, date of entry into force of the Constitution promulgated 27 October 1946. The end uses 3 October 1958 as the last full day before the 4 October 1958 promulgation of the Fifth Constitution, already represented by stable Fifth Republic Governance Context 078c50b9-4a15-46b4-9181-567cf07ee838. This is an exclusive-successor day-bound convention, not evidence that the Fourth Constitution was repealed precisely at midnight. De Gaulle's single 1 June 1958–8 January 1959 head-of-government Activity remains intact across the constitutional transition. No new sovereign Polity is asserted."
